# =============================================================================
#  MMC-MAD.orch - Multimodal Anonymous Dialogue
#  Workflow Description Language, AIF V3.0
#
#  THE USER AGENT NEVER ADDRESSES A MODULE. It asks the Controller to start one,
#  to take a datum for one, to give a datum from one, to stop one. The Module is
#  named in the request; the Controller is the party asked. Every line beginning
#  "ask Controller" is one call of the Controller API and nothing else is.
#
#      ask Controller to start  M              MPAI_AIFU_MODULE_Start
#      ask Controller to take   L (T[:n]) for M    MPAI_AIFU_MODULE_Input_Write
#      ask Controller to give   from M: L (T[:n])  MPAI_AIFU_MODULE_Output_Read
#      ask Controller to pause  M              MPAI_AIFU_MODULE_Pause
#      ask Controller to resume M              MPAI_AIFU_MODULE_Resume
#      ask Controller to stop   M              MPAI_AIFU_MODULE_Stop
#
#  A Port is addressed by its Data Type and, where a Module declares more than
#  one Port of that Data Type, its Port Number. The label before it is for the
#  reader and does not route.
# =============================================================================

workflow MMC-MAD over 1MMC-MAD-V2.5-I01, 1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01

on Start:

    # --- Welcome. A one-shot render, so its Module is started and stopped here.
    #     PAF-RSR declares TextObject twice: #1 feeds Text-To-Speech, #2 feeds
    #     Generative Face Description. Both are given or the face has nothing of
    #     the words to shape itself to.
    ask Controller to start 1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01
    ask Controller to take  Welcome (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1) = "Welcome to the MPAI
        Multimodal Conversation Service."
        for 1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01
    ask Controller to take  Welcome (OSD-BTO-V1.5:2) = "Welcome to the MPAI
        Multimodal Conversation Service."
        for 1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01
    ask Controller to give  from 1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01:
        WelcomeSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5),
        WelcomeFace   (PAF-FDO-V1.6)
    present WelcomeSpeech, WelcomeFace
    ask Controller to stop  1PAF-RSR-V1.6-I01

    # --- The dialogue. The Module lives from Start to Stop, so that Entity
    #     Dialogue Processing keeps the conversation's memory for the session.
    #     That memory is the Module's own: it is not a boundary datum and the
    #     User Agent neither holds it nor sees it.
    # THE WAIT IS THE APP'S TO EXPLAIN. Starting the Module loads speech
    # recognition and a language model on the Service, which takes a few seconds.
    # A person told nothing assumes a fault.
    prompt  "Loading the speech recogniser and the language model. This takes a
        few seconds."
    ask Controller to start 1MMC-MAD-V2.5-I01
    prompt  "Ready. Please begin - speak when you like."

    loop until Stop:
        acquire UserSpeech     (OSD-BSO-V1.5) via VAD

        ask Controller to take UserSpeech     (OSD-BSO-V1.5) for 1MMC-MAD-V2.5-I01

        ask Controller to give from 1MMC-MAD-V2.5-I01:
            MachineSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5),
            MachineFace   (PAF-FDO-V1.6)
        present MachineSpeech, MachineFace

on Stop:
    ask Controller to stop 1MMC-MAD-V2.5-I01
